<div class="default" align=center>
<strong>ASP Developer</strong></div>
<br>
<div class="default_9" align=justify>
<strong>Description</strong><br>
Functions / Responsibilities:<br>
<ol>
<li>Update and maintain current pages as needed to stay up to date with each of the games as they evolve.</li>
<li>Create new pages/scripts to interact with new information about the games or for new sites that will be added to the network.</li>
</ol>
Secondary Functions:<br>
Be available at odd times to help fix emergency errors that come up with databases.

<br><br>
<strong>Qualifications</strong><br>
Education and Training:<br>
Bachelor's Degree required. 4 years of related experience with 2 years of college would be an acceptable substitution.
<br><br>
Knowledge, Skills and Abilities:<br>
<ol>
<li>Significant experience programing in ASP is required.</li>
<li>Individual must be self-motivated. Ability to fulfill project tasks with minimal supervision required.</li>
<li>Ability to provide constructive feedback based upon logical reasoning required.</li>
<li>Effective verbal communication skills required. Effective written communication skills highly desired.</li>
<li>Familiarity with gaming industry in general is desired.</li>
</ol>
Other Requirements:
<ol>
<li>Individual must be located in the United States.</li>
<li>This is a part-time position that will vary in work load between 10-20 hours per week based upon current projects. As such, the individual can work from home and work around their existing schedule.</li>
<li>Applicant must have a Cell Phone be able to be reached in emergency situations. We do have other programers on staff and applicant would not be the first call in these situations.</li>
</ol>
The above is intended to describe the general content of and the requirements for satisfactory performance in this position. It is not to be construed as an exhaustive statement of the duties, responsibilities, or requirements of the position.
